course: dictionary
lesson: 5002
title: Industry: a whole group of businesses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «Software engineers work in almost every industry: banks, hospitals, farms, space, music, shops and governments.» The list after the colon gives examples, so industry here means an area of business.
explain: Industry can also mean making goods in factories, as in heavy industry. Ask what would fit in the sentence: "the factory of making cars" or "the business of making cars"? If your meaning makes sense, you have found it.
explain: The kind of text is a clue too. In a history book about the Industrial Revolution, industry means factories and machines. In a text about jobs, it usually means a group of businesses that do one kind of work.
explain: «Crunch is when game teams work very long hours before a deadline; it is common in parts of the industry...» Here the industry means the whole games business, not one factory or one shop.
fact: Industry means all the businesses that make or do one kind of thing, such as the car industry or the tourist industry.
fact: Heavy industry means making big, heavy goods in factories, such as steel or ships.
fact: Industry can also mean hard work, as in «a person of great industry», but this is a formal use.
fact: The Industrial Revolution was a time in history when factories and machines grew very quickly.
fact: An industry can have more than one: industries. Hard work, in the formal sense, has no plural.
exercise: «Software engineers work in almost every industry: banks, hospitals, farms, space, music, shops and governments.» What does industry mean here? | A small tool used in a workshop | A quiet, gloomy feeling | *An area of business, such as banks or farms | A type of sleepy weather
exercise: What does heavy industry mean? | *Making big goods in factories | Carrying heavy bags up the stairs | Working at home with the lights off | A very loud noise from a machine
exercise: «A person of great industry» is about a person who works very hard. Find and copy the word that means hard work. | person | great | *industry | of
test: «The film industry» is a phrase you may read in a newspaper. What does industry mean here? | A machine for making films | *All the businesses that make films | A film with a very long name | Hard work by one person
test: In «the Industrial Revolution», what does industry suggest? | *Factories and machines growing quickly | People stopping work for a holiday | Cold weather in the north | Everyone working in the fields
exam: What does industry mean in «the tourist industry brings visitors to the town»? | A quiet, sleepy place to stay | A tool for cleaning up rubbish | *All the businesses that serve tourists, such as hotels and tours | A special kind of tour guide
